Donald Trump has vetoed the second coronavirus&nbsp;
relief package that got through the House and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.920
Senate. And now there are immediately a number&nbsp;
of important things here. And let me get to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.920
what for many people is the most pressing and&nbsp;
important question. Does this mean that if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:27.280
were expecting a six hundred dollar check, if you&nbsp;
make up to seventy five thousand dollars a year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.720
that you will not be getting your six hundred&nbsp;
dollars? And the answer is, we can't say that yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.520
because this may be the first time that during&nbsp;
Donald Trump's presidency, the House and Senate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:41.600
are going to override Donald Trump's veto.&nbsp;
Remember that if a president vetoes a bill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.320
passed by the House and Senate, the House and&nbsp;
Senate can override that with a two thirds vote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.440
in the House and a two thirds vote in&nbsp;
the Senate. And that may well happen.&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.280
Reports are that the House will vote on&nbsp;
Monday and if the House votes to override,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:02.320
the Senate will reconvene on Tuesday to&nbsp;
vote as well. Now, the explanation for why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:08.000
Trump vetoed this bill is actually sort&nbsp;
of incoherent. Donald Trump with his veto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.320
notice, saying, quote, My administration has&nbsp;
taken strong actions to help keep our nation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:20.320
safe and support our service members. I will not&nbsp;
approve this bill, which would put the interests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:26.960
